course: dictionary
lesson: 790
title: Bedtime and the words around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Bedtime is a noun. It means the time when you usually go to bed. In «it's not fair... but at bedtime she said sorry», the clue is that bedtime is a time of day, not a place or a thing.
explain: Bedtime can also come before another word to describe things done just before sleeping, like a bedtime story. In «Lyra's mum says bedtime is 8», bedtime means the time itself. In «a later bedtime on Fridays at Gran's», it means the time you go to bed.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «At a sleepover the house rules belong to the host's parents, including bedtime.» Does "the time you usually go to bed" make sense there? Yes, so your meaning fits.
fact: Bedtime means the time when you usually go to bed.
fact: A bedtime story is a story read or told just before you sleep.
fact: A bedtime routine is the same things done in the same order each night, such as a bath, brushing teeth, pyjamas and a story.
fact: Children aged 9 to 10 usually need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep, so a regular bedtime helps.
fact: «Past your bedtime» means later than the time you should be in bed.
exercise: «Lyra's mum says bedtime is 8.» What does bedtime mean here? | The time you wake up | *The time you usually go to bed | A time of day when you go to bed | A bed made of wood
exercise: What is a bedtime story? | A story about beds | A long book for school | *A story read just before sleeping | A story told at breakfast
exercise: Children aged 9 to 10 usually need how many hours of sleep? | 1 hour | *9 to 12 hours | 6 to 7 hours | 14 to 16 hours
test: «Different houses can have different rules, like a later bedtime on Fridays at Gran's.» What does a later bedtime mean? | *Going to bed at a later time | A story told at night | Waking up earlier | Eating dinner later
test: Which phrase means later than you should be in bed? | Bedtime story | At bedtime | *Past your bedtime | Bedtime routine
exam: Jayden says, «Bedtime is when I go to sleep.» Is he right? | No, bedtime is a kind of bed | No, bedtime is a time for lunch | No, bedtime is only for grown-ups | *Yes, bedtime is the time you usually go to bed
